 and retention remain unchanged. The same query supplies cumulative raw main-turn counters from retained records, independent of context capacity, excluding sidecars and without the old statistics input-baseline subtraction. The label is recorded requests total, not an all-time invoice. Repeated or late seeds cannot overwrite a live main request. Optional/unavailable UsageStore support leaves the detail absent,
 and a delayed restore seed cannot replace any newer live main-request report.
 
+## Final Host request budget (K-07)
+
+The Host assembles MCP/discovered declarations and their Skill/context guidance before automatic
+compaction. Its immutable final tool set contributes name, description, input schema and strictness
+to the existing character estimate. Compaction retains the existing output reserve and failure
+limits; normal-turn output is capped against the same complete estimated input when positive
+space remains. A non-positive heuristic retains the existing provider-error recovery path. Unknown capacity
+remains unknown; the working fallback is never published as model evidence.
+
+Reported input already includes the preceding tool declarations. Existing assistant composition
+metadata therefore supplies the old declaration size, carried through live history and cold
+hydration without another store. A same-model provider anchor adds only the estimated declaration
+size difference and new history. This is a mixed estimate, never a new vendor measurement. Legacy
+records without composition use the larger of the complete local estimate and the reported-history
+floor; the missing old declaration size prevents an exact calibrated delta. Model changes use the
+complete local estimate. Raw input/output/cache counters and durable composition remain untouched.
+Compaction reprojects the same final tool guidance before the request; native executors keep their
+own compaction boundary.
+
+Compact-summary requests still use the original registry/count-based declaration selection;
+their own declaration budget is separate unfinished work. Changed system/Skill prefixes enter
+the complete local floor, but do not yet have a separate calibrated provider-anchor delta.
+
+Acceptance: isolated Host/Pi/SQLite requests cover first-request output reserve, dynamic discovery
+before compaction, tool growth/removal, unchanged declarations without double counting, cold
+composition restoration, sparse/zero capacities and unchanged vendor counters. These are local
+scripted-provider proofs; tokenizer accuracy and live vendor limits are not established.
+
 ## Small context compaction
 
 Keep the existing output reservation and token accounting. The default safety buffer is the smaller of 13K and 10% of the effective input window, so a small but positive window does not compact after a few tokens. Explicit buffer values (including zero) retain precedence. The 200K/1M defaults, disabled state and failure circuit breaker retain their behavior. A zero effective input budget is still a separate unresolved request-budget boundary; no artificial positive threshold is created. `packages/core/test/compact-policy.test.ts` covers the bounded change.
